# Copy to .env.local (git-ignored) for `pnpm dev`. Server-only: never prefix these with NEXT_PUBLIC_,
# which writes a value into the browser bundle. Under the AppHost, Aspire sets them for you.

# Where the support backend's API is, including the contract's /api prefix: the .NET API
# (http://127.0.0.1:5180/api) or the Python API run on its own (http://127.0.0.1:5280/api). The /api proxy
# reads it on every request, so one build runs against either: /api/v1/conversations -> {API_BASE_URL}/v1/conversations.
API_BASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:5180/api

# OpenTelemetry (src/instrumentation.ts): nothing is set up until an endpoint is set. Traces go over
# HTTP/protobuf to <endpoint>/v1/traces.
# OTEL_SERVICE_NAME=web
# OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ENDPOINT=https://collector.example.com
# OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_HEADERS=api-key=...
